@begin(section)

@title(Recipes)

For the impatient.

Make a bash script to wrap the dsolv binary like this, making sure to make
the script executable:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
#!/bin/sh
# Filename: /usr/bin/dsolv
exec <location-of-dsolv>/com.djhaskin.dsolv "${@}"
@end(code)

Generate a card:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
dsolv generate-card -i "name" -v "0.1.0" \
    -l "https://example.com/repo/name-0.1.0.zip" \
    -r "a-dep" -r "another-dep>=3.5.0" \
    -C name-0.1.0.zip.dscard
@end(code)

BASH: Download each location, then its signature, and verify it:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
#!/bin/sh
set -exou pipefail
dsolv resolve-locations -R ./index.dsrepo -r a -o json | \
    jq -r .packages[].location | \
    while read url
    do
        wget $url
        wget $url.asc
        gpg --verify $url.asc
    done
@end(code)

@end(section)
